# kex: check-only
# A module named like a type (`Time`) also answers that type's own functions,
# which its interface does not list, so its members went unchecked:
# `Time.monotonic`, which nothing declares, checked clean and was undefined on
# both backends. A name no function has anywhere is refused.

main do
  IO.inspect(Time.now)
  IO.inspect(Time.monotonic)
end
